itional households. Marriages succeed or fail based on communication, financial stability as a whole, and compatibility—not on which spouse's name is on the paycheck. So I'd hold your experience as a real caution—maybe it means you should go in eyes open about the specific stressors (in-law judgment being one, based on your own dad) rather than assuming it's a smooth path. But I wouldn't treat a handful of anecdotes as evidence that the arrangement itself is fundamentally unworkable. That's a bigger claim than the sample size can support.
